 "final_text": "`/work/mathd_numbertheory_314.lean` now compiles with no errors and no `sorry` warning.\n\nThe proof works by cases on the multiplier. Since `1342 \u2223 n`, write `n = 1342 * k`. Because `r = 1342 % 13 = 3`, the hypothesis `n % 13 < r` says `n % 13 < 3`.\n\nAssume for contradiction that `n < 6710`. Then `0 < k < 5`. For `k` from 1 to 4, `n % 13` is 3, 6, 9 and 12, and none of these is below 3. So `k \u2265 5` and `n \u2265 6710`.\n\nIn Lean this is `subst`, then `obtain \u27e8k, rfl\u27e9` on the divisibility, `by_contra`, bounds on `k` by `omega`, then `interval_cases k <;> omega`. Nothing else in the file was changed.",
